Translation patch: `RawBytes::as_bytes`

Change: `&self.0.as_ref()[..self.len()]` becomes `let len = self.len(); &self.0.as_ref()[..len]`.
Why: Aeneas fails ("Unreachable", InterpProjectors) when `self.len()` is called while the borrow returned by `as_ref` is live.
Behaviour: Identical: `len` and `as_ref` have no side effects, so the evaluation order does not matter.

diff --git a/src/misc/raw/bytes.rs b/src/misc/raw/bytes.rs
index d007086..3e13674 100644
--- a/src/misc/raw/bytes.rs
+++ b/src/misc/raw/bytes.rs
@@ -50,7 +50,8 @@ impl<'a, T: BytesRepr> RawBytes<'a, T> {
 
     /// Returns the _effective_ bytes (see `RawBytes::len`).
     pub fn as_bytes(&self) -> &[u8] {
-        &self.0.as_ref()[..self.len()]
+        let len = self.len();
+        &self.0.as_ref()[..len]
     }
 
     /// Returns the value as a UTF-8 string (lossy converted).
